{"type":"message","id":"947df011","parentId":"5a82e718","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:51:50.551Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should flag that this is a behavior change worth noting: inputs with Z now produce timezone-aware datetimes, so comparing them against naive ones would raise an error.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with a fixed format. That format had no way to handle the trailing `Z`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\nOne behaviour change: timestamps ending in `Z` now come back with a UTC timezone attached (`tzinfo=timezone.utc`). Timestamps without `Z` still come back with no timezone, as before. If any code compares or subtracts a result from each kind, Python will raise a `TypeError`. `day_key` isn't affected, and it's the only other caller in the repo.\n\n`fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 or later; this environment runs 3.13."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":297,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26949,"totalTokens":27248,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":26949}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277506405,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dRzYEQVjkjMtnBV3nx","duration":4136.781752000003,"ttft":1447.7732240000005,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26951,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
